# Portfolio Project

Vite + React 18 portfolio for Pavlo Pikalov. Hosted on GitHub Pages user site at `https://pavlopikalov.github.io/`.

## Stack

- React 18, React Router 6, Vite 5, SCSS modules (`*.module.scss`)
- No TypeScript, no CSS-in-JS, no global component libraries

## Key paths

- Routes: `src/App.jsx` — `BrowserRouter` with no basename (user-site repo)
- Vite base: `vite.config.js` — `base: '/'`
- Pages: `src/pages/{Home,Projects,About,Contact}/`
- Shared UI: `src/components/`
- Static assets: `public/` (e.g. `cv.pdf`)

## Conventions

- Functional components only; colocate `Component.jsx` + `Component.module.scss`
- Mobile-first SCSS; tablet/desktop breakpoint: `@media (min-width: 768px)`
- Semantic HTML, ARIA labels on interactive elements, meaningful `alt` on images
- Keep SEO-friendly markup: one `h1` per page section, descriptive headings

## Deploy

- Auto-deploy: push to `production` → `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
- GitHub Pages source must be **GitHub Actions** (not `gh-pages` branch)
- SPA fallback: build copies `index.html` → `404.html` in CI

## Do not change without reason

- `base` / `basename` / `package.json` `homepage` — all must stay aligned for GitHub Pages
- Do not add heavy dependencies for simple UI needs
